# native_reclass.lst -- the corpus rows whose native FAIL is reclassified, and
# what proves them natively instead (#143 A14b, phase-5 review finding 2).
#   <row> | <class> | <native proof>
# A class in native_judge.py's RULES reclassifies a FAIL as SKIP only when the
# FAILURE REASON matches the class's rule; a class in SCRIPTED replaces the row
# by a per-row native script's result, which must be PASS.
